@startuml
namespace core <<component>> {
    namespace Module <<unit>> {
        class "Worker"
    }
    namespace Other <<unit>> {
        class "Worker"
    }
}
' This negative case declares Worker twice with the same canonical id.
' To show Module and Other using one shared Worker, declare it once in the
' overview and express usage through relationships, not duplicate declarations.
' See the recommended organization in:
' plantuml/parser/integration_test/class_diagram/grouping_containers_overview_dependencies
' That example shows both Clients depending on the shared Worker.
@enduml
